# The register and the supplier's own GSTR-1 declare the **same invoice with
# different values** — Plan 108 Slice 5.
#
# **`AmountMismatch` compares the register against GSTR-2B; this compares it
# against what the supplier actually declared, and the difference matters for
# whose mistake it is.** A disagreement with 2B can be caused by the authority
# not having received the line at all. A disagreement with GSTR-1 cannot: both
# sides are asserting a figure about the same invoice, so one of the two is
# wrong, and the finding names both so a reviewer can tell which.
#
# **The cap is read from the graph, exactly as `amount-mismatch.sparql` reads
# it**, and for the same reason: a tolerance hardcoded here would report a
# compliant 2020 invoice as a finding every month. Amending the law is adding
# a subject to `law/rule-36-4.ttl`, and the citation travels with the row so a
# reviewer sees which notification the judgement was made under.
#
# **Scoped to `taxableValue` for this first cut**, matching `AmountMismatch`'s
# own scope. Invoice-number, date and tax-head diffing are real and are
# deliberately a later slice — bundling them here would mean one finding with
# four possible meanings, which is the thing this plan exists to undo.
#
# "Latest provision in force" is `OPTIONAL` + `!BOUND`, not `FILTER NOT
# EXISTS` — see `amount-mismatch.sparql` for why that distinction is not
# stylistic.

PREFIX gst: <https://graph-owl.dev/packs/gst#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

SELECT ?purchase ?number ?gstin ?claimed ?declaredValue ?capPercent ?citation
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?register {
    ?purchase a gst:PurchaseInvoice ;
              gst:issuedBy ?supplier ;
              gst:invoiceNumber ?number ;
              gst:invoiceDate   ?date ;
              gst:taxableValue  ?claimed .
    ?supplier gst:supplierGstin ?gstin .
  }

  GRAPH ?gstr1 {
    ?declared a gst:Gstr1Invoice ;
              gst:issuedBy ?declaredSupplier ;
              gst:invoiceNumber ?number ;
              gst:taxableValue  ?declaredValue .
    ?declaredSupplier gst:supplierGstin ?gstin .
  }

  # The provision in force on the invoice date.
  GRAPH ?law {
    ?provision a gst:Provision ;
               gst:effectiveFrom ?from ;
               gst:capPercent    ?capPercent ;
               gst:citation      ?citation .
  }
  FILTER (?from <= ?date)

  # …and no later one that had also taken effect by then.
  OPTIONAL {
    GRAPH ?laterLaw {
      ?later a gst:Provision ;
             gst:effectiveFrom ?laterFrom .
    }
    FILTER (?laterFrom <= ?date && ?laterFrom > ?from)
  }
  FILTER (!BOUND(?later))

  FILTER (
    ABS(xsd:decimal(?claimed) - xsd:decimal(?declaredValue))
      > xsd:decimal(?claimed) * xsd:decimal(?capPercent) / 100
  )
}
ORDER BY ?number
